Explanation:

In seawater at pH 8.1, the carbonate equilibrium maintains $approx 90%$ as bicarbonate ($HCO_3^-$), $approx 9-10%$ as carbonate ($CO_3^(2-)$), and $<1%$ as dissolved aqueous $CO_2$.
